    "created_at": "2026-08-02T21:17:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-02T21:17:02Z",
    "body": "A reserved Windows device name turning an rd on one folder into an rd on the whole drive is a genuinely nasty bypass, the target path looks completely ordinary right up until Windows resolves it. Pattern-matching a destructive command guard against the literal path string an agent submits (immunity-agent does this, github.com/PrismorSec/prismor) would not have caught this either, the string it saw was a scoped subdirectory, the catastrophic part only happened during OS-level path resolution downstream of that string. The background task continuing after Esc is arguably the sharper bug here, a guard that blocks the initial call does nothing once execution has already started.",
